4. Third-party code  --  keeps its own license
   - ST HAL and LL drivers, CMSIS device files, USB device core and middleware
     under stm32u5a5-keypad/firmware/Drivers and stm32u5a5-keypad/firmware/USB:
     STMicroelectronics licenses (BSD-3-Clause or SLA0044 as stated in the
     LICENSE.md and file headers in those folders) and Apache-2.0 for the Arm
     CMSIS core headers (LICENSE.txt in that folder). Keep those notices.
   - Files copied from the same ST packages inside future_work/ and archive/
     carry the same ST license.
   - The RP2040 proof-of-concept files in the top level (proofofconcept.c,
     config.h, mcuconf.h, rules.mk, keyboard.json, keymaps/, mux_analog.*,
     pio_uart.*) are written for the QMK firmware framework, which is licensed
     GPL-2.0-or-later. Treat those files as GPL-2.0-or-later, not MIT, unless a
     file says otherwise. The keymap file carries an SPDX line saying so.
   - The BLE and ESB bridge sketches use Arduino and Nordic libraries under
     their own licenses; follow the headers of those libraries.

